/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 347 0 R
/E (Revenue. Consolidated revenue is projected to grow from VND 32.7 trillion in 2025 to VND 47.2 trillion by 2030 \(Figure 32\), driven by M&C backlog execution, FSO fleet expansion with new entrants and Port & Base activity  being renewed by the next O&G and wind cycle M&C revenue.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 347 0 R
/E (Cost: Our projection focuses on fluctuations in variable costs, specifically structural steel prices and offshore vessel chartering rates. Meanwhile, fixed costs from FSO/FPSO and port infrastructure depreciation will remain stable as % of sales, driven by economies of scale from mega-project backlogs \(Block B - O Mon, Lac Da Vang\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 347 0 R
/E (Gross Margin: PVS's blended gross margin is structurally bounded in the 4-6% range, reflecting its project contractor and asset operator model \(Figure 32\). Margins compress to 4.4% in FY2028 at the peak of Block B offshore installation, before recovering to 4.6-4.8% as the mix shifts toward domestic offshore wind EPCI from FY2029.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [15]
>>
