/S /H1
/P 358 0 R
/T (Bear case: PVS faces macro and project-level headwinds that compress margins and defer revenue realisation. Rising labour, materials, and subcontractor costs cannot be fully passed through under fixed-price EPC contracts, causing gross margin to decline to 4.25% and EBITDA margin to 3.00%. Brent crude sustained below USD 70/bbl prompts PVN to exercise budgetary restraint, reducing new tender flow and intensifying price competition among domestic EPC contractors. Elevated risk premium and tighter liquidity push WACC to 11.67% and trim terminal growth to 5.00%, implying 28,640 VND/share \(-24.63%\).)
/E (Bear case: PVS faces macro and project-level headwinds that compress margins and defer revenue realisation. Rising labour, materials, and subcontractor costs cannot be fully passed through under fixed-price EPC contracts, causing gross margin to decline to 4.25% and EBITDA margin to 3.00%. Brent crude sustained below USD 70/bbl prompts PVN to exercise budgetary restraint, reducing new tender flow and intensifying price competition among domestic EPC contractors. Elevated risk premium and tighter liquidity push WACC to 11.67% and trim terminal growth to 5.00%, implying 28,640 VND/share \(-24.63%\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 358 0 R
/T (Bull case: PVS benefits from a favourable upstream investment cycle underpinned by Brent above USD 85/bbl and accelerated PVN capital deployment. PVS wins incremental international tenders and expands its JV pipeline, capitalising on the regional energy transition capex wave. A more accommodative rate environment compresses WACC to 9.67%, while terminal growth is maintained at 8.00%, consistent with PVS's alignment with Vietnam's National Energy Master Plan. The combined effect implies 53,873 VND/share \(+41.77%\).)
/E (Bull case: PVS benefits from a favourable upstream investment cycle underpinned by Brent above USD 85/bbl and accelerated PVN capital deployment. PVS wins incremental international tenders and expands its JV pipeline, capitalising on the regional energy transition capex wave. A more accommodative rate environment compresses WACC to 9.67%, while terminal growth is maintained at 8.00%, consistent with PVS's alignment with Vietnam's National Energy Master Plan. The combined effect implies 53,873 VND/share \(+41.77%\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
