3246 0 obj
<<
/Title ([O1] - EPC/EPCI Contract Execution Risk: Under lump-sum EPCI structures, cost escalation and schedule overruns are absorbed entirely by PVS - a structural hazard of the industry that the majority of offshore projects miss sanctioned cost and schedule targets at completion \(Appendix 24, Appendix 25\). Valuation: A 2pp EBITDA margin compression from a single mid-size overrun reduces our target price by 1.75%. Mitigation: Tighten subcontractor pre-qualification and progress toward Target Cost/Gain-Share structures on technically novel contracts, supported by comprehensive project insurance \(performance bond, marine all-risk\).)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2930 0 R
/First 3390 0 R
/Last 3390 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 3391 0 R
>>
endobj
3247 0 obj
<<
/Title (Bear case: PVS faces macro and project-level headwinds that compress margins and defer revenue realisation. Rising labour, materials, and subcontractor costs cannot be fully passed through under fixed-price EPC contracts, causing gross margin to decline to 4.25% and EBITDA margin to 3.00%. Brent crude sustained below USD 70/bbl prompts PVN to exercise budgetary restraint, reducing new tender flow and intensifying price competition among domestic EPC contractors. Elevated risk premium and tighter liquidity push WACC to 11.67% and trim terminal growth to 5.00%, implying 28,640 VND/share \(-24.63%\).)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3392 0 R
/First 3393 0 R
/Last 3394 0 R
/Count -6
/Next 2931 0 R
>>
endobj
